=====Usage notes=====
The optional acute accent in {{m|nb|én}} distinguishes stressed numerical “one” from the unstressed article. The corresponding feminine spelling is {{m|nb|éi}}. In the neuter, stressed {{m|nb|ett}} contrasts with unstressed {{m|nb|et}}; the choice can depend on emphasis, including in expressions such as ''et(t) eller annet'' and ''et(t) eneste''. The definite form is {{m|nb|ene}}, as in ''den ene boka'' (“the one book”) or ''den ene og den andre'' (“the one and the other”).<ref>{{cite-web|url=https://sprakradet.no/spraksporsmal-og-svar/et-eller-ett/|title=Et eller ett?|work=Språkrådet|date=2024-01-01|accessdate=2026-10-27}}</ref>

