=====Usage notes=====
{{m|nb|en|En}} is used with masculine nouns and can also be used with feminine nouns; {{m|nb|ei}} is the specifically feminine form, and {{m|nb|et}} is neuter. Unlike numerical “one”, the article is normally unstressed. A bare occupational or classificatory noun can occur without it after a verb such as {{m|nb|være}}: ''hun er lærer'' (“she is a teacher”). It is normally present when that noun is characterized: ''hun er en god lærer'' (“she is a good teacher”).

